{%- comment -%}
  The Pair's figures, worked out from the products' own prices and the
  saving in Theme settings > Offers (which mirrors the pair discount), so
  copy that quotes them stays right when a price changes. This is the one
  place the theme turns those settings into money.

    {% render 'pair-price' %}               -> the pair price   ("$47")
    {% render 'pair-price', part: 'full' %} -> one of each, at full price ("$55")
    {% render 'pair-price', part: 'save' %} -> the saving       ("$8")

  Write [pair_price] in a theme text setting (announcement claim, button
  label) and the section renders it through this snippet:
    {%- capture pp -%}{% render 'pair-price' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {{ s.claim | replace: '[pair_price]', pp | escape }}

  Renders nothing when the pair is not set up, or when the visitor sees a
  currency other than the shop's: the saving is a fixed amount in the shop's
  currency that Shopify converts at checkout, so a figure worked out here in
  another currency would not be the one the bag shows. Callers treat an
  empty result as "say it without a number".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pa = settings.pair_product_a
  assign pb = settings.pair_product_b
  if settings.pair_enabled and cart.currency.iso_code == shop.currency and pa != blank and pb != blank and pa.price != blank and pb.price != blank
    assign full = pa.price | plus: pb.price
    case part
      when 'full'
        echo full | money_without_trailing_zeros
      when 'save'
        echo settings.pair_save_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
      else
        assign pp = full | minus: settings.pair_save_cents
        echo pp | money_without_trailing_zeros
    endcase
  endif
-%}
